-- title:
--   W[[u,v]]/(uv-π) is local for π a non-unit
-- statement:
--   Let $W$ be a commutative ring which is a local ring (in the Mathlib sense: nontrivial, with the non-units forming an ideal), and let $\pi \in W$ be an element that is not a unit. Write $\mathrm{uvCrossingIdeal}\,W\,\pi$ for the ideal of the two-variable power series ring $\mathrm{MvPowerSeries}\,(\mathrm{Fin}\,2)\,W$ generated by the single element $X_0 X_1 - C(\pi)$, where $X_0, X_1$ are the two power series variables and $C(\pi)$ is the constant series with value $\pi$, and let $\mathrm{UVCrossingModel}\,W\,\pi$ be the quotient ring $\mathrm{MvPowerSeries}\,(\mathrm{Fin}\,2)\,W / (X_0X_1 - C(\pi))$, i.e. $W[[u,v]]/(uv-\pi)$. The assertion is that this quotient ring is again a local ring.
--
--   This is the statement that the crossing model $W[[u,v]]/(uv-\pi)$, which arises as the completed local ring of a modular curve at a point where the special fibre acquires an ordinary double point (for $W$ a Witt ring and $\pi = p$, as in the Deligne–Rapoport description of $M_{\Gamma_0(p)}$ at a supersingular point), is local. It is used throughout the project wherever such crossing models appear as local charts or as prorepresenting rings of deformation functors, for instance in the construction of surjections onto $\mathrm{UVCrossingModel}$ from deformation rings and in the identification of adic completions of blow-up charts.
-- source:
